# Deployment logs

Focus the log pane, then use the wheel or **PageUp**/**PageDown**. The pane
consumes movement until it reaches a boundary; remaining rows scroll this
document so the runbook below comes into view.

::input{id="filter" label="Filter" placeholder="service or message"}

:::scroll{id="logs" rows="9"}
```text
14:02:01 api      release 2026.07.27 queued
14:02:02 worker   draining 42 jobs
14:02:03 api      artifact signature verified
14:02:04 web      health check passed
14:02:05 worker   queue drained
14:02:06 api      migrating session cache
14:02:07 web      warming edge cache
14:02:08 api      canary receiving 5% traffic
14:02:09 metrics  p95 latency 84ms
14:02:10 metrics  error rate 0.02%
14:02:11 api      canary promoted to 50%
14:02:12 worker   resumed jobs
14:02:13 web      cache hit ratio 96%
14:02:14 api      deployment complete
14:02:15 audit    rollout approved by Ada
```
:::

::checkbox{id="follow" label="Follow new entries" checked="true"}

::button{id="close" label="Close"}

## Rollout runbook

1. Confirm latency and error-rate budgets.
2. Compare canary and baseline traffic.
3. Verify workers have resumed.
4. Record the release owner and approval.
